{"text": "* \" \\INBIFO Institut fiir biologische Forschung-K\u00e9in\n\ni\n\n\u201csmoke of the standard\n\n===Please cut here-\u2014~\n\nDr. T.S. Osdene, Director of Research\n\nTelex No. 2096 September 28, 1979 DRRS/HKL/RB\n\n: Copy Wo.:10 4\n\nPROPOSAL A 0500/3018\n\n91 D-SMOKE INHALATION STUDY ON MALE RATS,\n\nRESPONSE OF BIOASSAYS TO SUB~ACUTE INHALATION AND RECOVERY\n\nProject leader: Dr. W. Reininghaus\n\nAss. project leader: J. Kiihd\n\n1 INTRODUCTION\n\nThis 90 d-smoke inhalation study on male rats is designed to\ninvestigate the response of established bioassays to diluted\nrence cigarette 2R1 in an acute and\nsub-acute inhalation. The study includes the investigation of\nrecovery after 14 and 50 days of exposure.\n\n\u2018he following bioassays are applied in this study:\n\n1 induction of AdM activity and o-demethylase activity in the\nkidney and the lavesed lung.\n\n2 phagoluminescence and phagocytosis of free lung celis\n\n3 activity of serum aminotransferases and serum glucose\nconcentration\n\n4 number and proportion of different types of free lung cells\n5 histology of the respiratory tract\n\u2018he time dependence of responses will be studied by testing\n\nafter 7, 14 and 91 days of inhalation and after a 7 day\nrecovery period following 14 and 91 days of inhalation.\n\nEqual numbers of rats are randomly allocated to 1 sham exposure\n{o-GR) and 2 smoke exposure groups (1-GR and 2-GR). A 4th smoke\nexposure group (3-GR) will be sacrificed after 14 days of inhal-\nation plus the additional 7 d recovery period.\n\nSSZES06202", "words": [{"text": "*", "x0": 81, "y0": 30, "x1": 84, "y1": 33, "conf": 32.0}, {"text": "\"", "x0": 95, "y0": 30, "x1": 97, "y1": 32, "conf": 11.0}, {"text": "\\INBIFO", "x0": 108, "y0": 33, "x1": 157, "y1": 47, "conf": 9.0}, {"text": "Institut", "x0": 161, "y0": 26, "x1": 202, "y1": 51, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "fiir", "x0": 208, "y0": 26, "x1": 225, "y1": 51, "conf": 90.0}, {"text": "biologische", "x0": 231, "y0": 26, "x1": 30